{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017BPt5Tm1fVSpJ3qG7Pa4Pf","type":"tool_result","content":"470\t  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n471\t- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n472\t  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n473\t  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n474\t  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n475\t  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n476\t- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n477\t  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n478\t  NFKC form.\n479\t- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main\n480\t  checkout is on a feature branch.\n481\t- `ceo-restore.sh` previews by default; pass `--apply` to restore. Keep your\n482\t  own copy of `audit-key` and `.salt`, because the backup leaves them out.\n483\t- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n484\t  run on them, check the `model:` of your agent files yourself.\n485\t- The model allowlist now admits other vendors' ids (Gemini, Grok) and\n486\t  retired Claude 4 ids. `/ceo-boot` no longer reports a model variable set\n487\t  to one of them as `settings_tamper_model_remap`, and `validate-governance.sh`\n488\t  accepts such a `model:` in an agent file. If you rely on that tamper\n489\t  finding, check the model variables of your settings yourself."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8251238c-5deb-4f64-879e-480beb36292d","uuid":"91a3c397-5243-47ea-b3d4-8214f5f3a94e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:41:44.474Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n  NFKC form.\n- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main\n  checkout is on a feature branch.\n- `ceo-restore.sh` previews by default; pass `--apply` to restore. Keep your\n  own copy of `audit-key` and `.salt`, because the backup leaves them out.\n- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n  run on them, check the `model:` of your agent files yourself.\n- The model allowlist now admits other vendors' ids (Gemini, Grok) and\n  retired Claude 4 ids. `/ceo-boot` no longer reports a model variable set\n  to one of them as `settings_tamper_model_remap`, and `validate-governance.sh`\n  accepts such a `model:` in an agent file. If you rely on that tamper\n  finding, check the model variables of your settings yourself.","numLines":20,"startLine":470,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017BPt5Tm1fVSpJ3qG7Pa4Pf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
