{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1GGZNeRDdE9cFq6bi1v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qz8WfaKDiw2pA87N4eaHHP","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 6/32: the ten new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/, which hold the ceo-boot.py logic split out by PLAN-197.\n\nWHAT WAS VERIFIED AND HOLDS\n- How the parts load. ceo-boot.py:114-116 calls install(globals()), and _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:20-26 compiles each part under its real filename and runs it in the facade's own namespace. As a result:\n  - \"global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE\" (state_plan_audit.py) still rebinds the facade's variable.\n  - Monkeypatch points such as module._get_plan_paths and AUDIT_LOG_DEFAULT are still looked up in the facade.\n  - Path(__file__) resolves to .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py, the facade's __file__. So morning_ledger.py, lessons.py, persona_demand_resolver.py, persona_demand_scan.py and check-confidence-gate-drift.py resolve where they did before, and parents[2] is still the repo root. All five files exist in .claude/scripts/.\n- Load order. Everything evaluated while a part loads exists by then:\n  - FAILOPEN_RAIL_CLASSIFIERS needs _classify_pair_rail_event, defined in persona_confidence, which loads before liveness_schedule.\n  - TIER_S_CHECKS needs check_governance_validate, which the facade defines at ceo-boot.py:70, before install.\n  - The _UNSET default in lessons_cli needs candidates_lessons, which loads first.\n  - No two parts define the same top-level name.\n- Python 3.9 and the standard library. The parts import nothing outside the standard library and the repo's own _lib. They use shutdown(cancel_futures=True), which needs 3.9 or later, and string annotations. Nothing newer than 3.9.\n- Delivery. install_lib_selective (scripts/install.sh:1520-1550) copies every top-level _lib entry except the test harness, so the subpackage reaches fresh installs. The upgrade manifest walks the whole .claude/hooks tree. The canonical guard \".claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py\" (canonical_edit/guards.py:34) covers the parts.\n- Fail direction. Advisory checks fail open. The boot-lesson render gate (candidates_lessons.py _validate_boot_lesson) fails closed when the validator is missing or raises; that is a security matcher on input, which is the right direction. No inversion found.\n- Adopter impact. The only new check is main_checkout_state, and it is yellow only, which does not change gate_pass. CHANGELOG lines 340 and 479 declare it. In this payload, nothing disables hooks, changes the model or effort, or blocks a session.\n- Declared conditions. None is contradicted by this payload. Condition 7 holds: ceo-boot.py keeps its path and its logic moves to _lib.\n\nNO P0. NO NEW P1.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:304\n- What breaks: _sentinel_patterns() AST-parses .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py for _PATTERNS. After the PLAN-197 split, that file is a thin entry point, and _PATTERNS now lives in .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238. So the function always falls back (lines 308 and 325).\n- Effect: sentinels_pending_gpg scans 4 of the 10 sentinel locations the guard trusts. It no longer sees architect/wave-0a, wave-0b, wave-1-2, wave-minus-1, staging/review and audit-v2/architect/round-*. A pending sentinel at one of those still-trusted locations is never surfaced.\n- The degradation is visible: every boot, in the meta repo and in every install, the summary carries \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\" (line 356). That is the noise that trains operators to ignore the line.\n- The S321 comment's claim that the patterns are \"EXTRAÍDOS por AST do arquivo que os define\" is now false.\n- Minimal fix: point src_path at _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py, or try both files. Add a test that asserts derived is True on the real tree.\n\nP2-2 Duplicate check function, and guards bound to the facade instead of the parts\n- What happens: ceo-boot.py:120 redefines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift after install(). But TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py:373-376) was built while the parts loaded, so dispatch runs the copy in model_persona.py:6. The two bodies are identical today, so behavior is unchanged, but the facade copy is dead code in production.\n- Why it matters:\n  - The S287 regression test extracts the function from ceo-boot.py by AST (scripts/tests/test_check_vacuous_checks.py, _extract_spec_drift_fn). It therefore tests the copy dispatch never runs.\n  - check-vacuous-checks.py defaults to ceo-boot.py only (line 133). That file now holds 2 check_* functions; about 35 moved to the parts and escape the vacuity lint.\n  - The facade docstring \"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\" has nothing to do with this function. It appears to exist only to keep a source-grep assertion green (test_check_vacuous_checks.py:306).\n  - The marker comments at ceo-boot.py:180-184 likewise satisfy source-grep tests (test_plan_091_expected_callsites, test_ceo_boot_audit_emit:95) through comments, not code.\n- Minimal fix: delete the facade duplicate. Point the lint default and those tests at _ceo_boot_parts/*.py, or at the TIER_A_CHECKS entry. Drop the unrelated docstring.\n\nP2-3 Every part (line 1 of each file)\n- Each part opens with a module docstring. Running it in the facade namespace rebinds ceo_boot.__doc__ to \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\", replacing the operator docstring. One more instance of \"same text, different behavior\".\n- The parts also cannot be imported on their own: they reference re, List and _UNSET from the facade and raise NameError. No current tool imports every _lib module, so nothing breaks today.\n- Minimal fix: remove the part docstrings, or restore __doc__ after install. Add a comment in __init__.py that the parts are not importable.\n\nP2-4 .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py:241\n- What breaks: when refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is absent, main_checkout_state assumes the default branch is \"main\".\n- Effect: an adopter whose default branch is master or trunk and who has no origin/HEAD (a repo made with git init and remote add) gets a permanent false yellow. It is advisory only.\n- Minimal fix: if origin/HEAD is missing, report green \"default branch unknown\", or read init.defaultBranch.\n\nP2-5 Documentation gap (CHANGELOG [1.4.4], lines 110-125 and 471)\n- What changed: the ceo-boot logic moved from a non-canonical path (.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py, absent from _CANONICAL_GUARDS) to a canonical one (_lib/**/*.py). Editing it now needs an Owner sentinel.\n- Effect: an adopter who customized ceo-boot.py and follows the CHANGELOG's \"re-apply the patch to the module\" hits the canonical-edit wall when an agent tries it.\n- Minimal fix: add one CHANGELOG line saying that the ceo-boot modules are sentinel-gated.","decision":"GO","sentence":"This payload contradicts no declared condition and has no P0 or P1: the split preserves global lookup, loading order, the delivery path and the fail direction, and the problems found are P2 follow-ups, among them a sentinel-pattern lookup stuck on its fallback (it says so on every boot) and test guards bound to a facade copy that dispatch never runs."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3276,"cache_read_input_tokens":214570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3276},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8251238c-5deb-4f64-879e-480beb36292d","uuid":"a89f0711-cf30-4d43-b0c5-0f08ac270291","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:45:01.413Z","request_id":"